<x-legal-document title="Terms of Service" updated="27 September 2026">
    <p>These terms cover using Ihsan, whether you are giving to an organization or raising funds as one. By giving through the platform, or by opening an organization account, you accept them.</p>

    <h2>What Ihsan is</h2>
    <p>Ihsan is a platform that lets registered Malaysian organizations collect donations. Your donation is made to that organization, not to Ihsan. We take the payment on their behalf, pass the funds to them, and give them the tools to account for it. What an organization does with the money is a matter between you and them.</p>
    <p>We check that an organization is registered before approving it, but we do not audit how funds are spent.</p>

    <h2>Making a donation</h2>
    <p>A donation is charged to your card at the moment you confirm it. You may be offered a currency other than ringgit; the amount shown in ringgit is an estimate at the day's rate, and the amount your bank charges may differ slightly.</p>
    <p>You may choose to cover the transaction costs. When you do, that amount is added to your donation and pays the processing and platform fees, so the organization receives the full sum you intended.</p>

    <h2>Recurring gifts</h2>
    <p>A monthly or yearly gift charges the card you saved, on the same day of each period, until you stop it. We email a receipt after every successful charge, so each installment is accounted for.</p>
    <p>If an installment fails, we try again on a schedule — after one day, then three, then seven, then seven again. If a whole round of attempts fails, the cycle repeats. After four failed rounds the plan stops and we stop charging you. You can stop a plan yourself at any time from the link in your receipt, or by asking the organization.</p>

    <h2>Fees</h2>
    <p>Ihsan charges the organization a platform fee on each donation, and the payment processor charges its own fee. Both are deducted from the donation before the organization receives it, unless you chose to cover them. The rates in force are set out in each organization's agreement with us.</p>

    <h2>Refunds</h2>
    <p>A refund is the organization's decision, not ours: they received the donation. Ask them first. We will carry out a refund they approve, and it returns to the card you paid with. Processing fees already charged are not returned.</p>

    <h2>Receipts</h2>
    <p>We email a receipt for every successful donation, from the organization, carrying its registration details. Whether a receipt is tax-deductible depends on the organization's own status with the Inland Revenue Board, and is stated on the receipt itself.</p>

    <h2>If you are an organization</h2>
    <p>You undertake that your registration details are true, that your campaigns describe honestly what the money is for, and that you will use funds for the purpose you stated. You are responsible for what your campaign pages say and for answering your donors.</p>
    <p>We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms, that we are required to act against, or that puts donors at risk. Where we do, funds already collected are passed on or returned as the circumstances require.</p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>We work to keep the platform available and accurate, but we do not guarantee it will be uninterrupted or error-free. We are not liable for what an organization does with a donation, nor for losses beyond the fees we charged on the donation in question, except where the law does not allow that limit.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Malaysia, and the Malaysian courts have jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.</p>

    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>If these terms change we will update the date at the top of this page. A donation is governed by the terms in force on the day it was made.</p>
